From: danprice142 <danprice142@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:25:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] renderer_opengl: fixes for Mesa's D3D12 OpenGL driver

- Identify Mesa's D3D12 driver (vendor Microsoft / Mesa) so native AMD and
  Intel workarounds are not applied to it.
- Tolerate drivers that report no program-binary formats or return no
  usable binary: keep the GLSL disk cache and rebuild from source.
- Compile shaders on the render thread when a shared context can't be made,
  and don't create idle worker contexts.
- Skip the second-layer opacity setup when the layer is fully opaque.

From danprice142's Azahar-UWP (https://github.com/danprice142/Azahar-UWP).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GBZiGZJLWikH7o79f84GTm
